# What must never reach GitHub: signing material, build output, local machine state.
#
# Everything in this repository is either documentation, the patch against upstream, or the
# Android shell crate itself. None of it is secret, and none of it is generated.

# Signing material — the one thing here that could cost someone their upload key, and the one
# thing that must never be committed by accident. `scripts/build-apk.sh` expects a keystore
# under a path outside the checkout (android-tools/<app>-sideload.keystore) precisely so it
# cannot land here.
*.jks
*.keystore
*.p12
*.pfx
*.pem
*.der
*.key
*.csr
keystore.properties
key.properties
signing.properties
release.keystore.properties
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# Build output.
target/
**/target/
build/
.gradle/
*.apk
*.aab
*.apks
*.ap_
*.idsig
*.dex
*.class
*.jar
!gradle/wrapper/gradle-wrapper.jar

# Local machine state. `local.properties` points at an SDK path, `*.sh` scripts are sourced
# from an environment this repository does not carry, and logs are the app's own runtime trace
# (a file in the app's data directory on the device, or dropped here by hand while debugging).
local.properties
android-sdk/
android-ndk/
*.log
logs/

# Editor and IDE state.
.idea/
*.iml
.vscode/
.fleet/
*.swp
*~
*.bak
*.orig
*.rej

# Operating system debris.
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini
$RECYCLE.BIN/